I55KmriOTZ9rgRxA0E6RzQv9DtWT6tLkXpZn-iOIb0_QHqa24JShlfqhlLEqCkLP-Z0pYlVeUAeHvmSVoQKsTdaz-rnCaSY2MSQkOoznonb1Vj_0urLcorWyElZ1MZFkVQ9Z0njnGI_YXrM_29EEBE69bkIfLdM_NmwwkjLYh_oCq3oaVHwRNGiSRRQPo_m_U7JzyLHp0RSsPr82FkhpatUtshl4KWPxdN4ygRvyGn3Ge3CS0-NFMStvQ6bNWF81zwFeMwikRt_7_-QZ7BQYyhQOa2mKSfzbjrzI6TtYLKhWdaNHIOSM857x3wN0TOJtMpmANtCX_4yz00H34tjxt7bR9gYmYWM5AnQOEhh1VLg==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Preparing for sales call**\\n\\nI need to prepare the answer for the user's request regarding the sales call for Exoscale. It's important to consider asking for the context of the company or their specific needs. I should provide general positions and clarification points, perhaps in a French-style tone due to potential typos. \\n\\nI'll aim for concise bullet points and use a straightforward, caveman-like approach, but since the user wrote informally, I can keep it simple yet effective!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Good move to prep before sales call.\n\n## Position to take (you)\n**Goal:** get facts, not get sold.  \nYou friendly, curious, but strict on requirements + numbers.\n\nUse this posture:\n- “We evaluating fit for production workloads.”\n- “Need technical + commercial clarity before any commitment.”\n- “If fit good, we can run pilot fast.”\n\n---\n\n## Key points to clarify with Exoscale sales\n\n### 1) Business / contract\n- Pricing model (compute, storage, bandwidth, managed services)\n- Hidden costs (egress, snapshots, support tiers, IPs)\n- Discount options (annual commit, startup credits, volume)\n- Contract flexibility (monthly vs yearly, termination terms)\n\n### 2) Infrastructure fit\n- Regions available (and roadmap)\n- Data residency / sovereignty (EU/CH constraints?)\n- SLA per service (VM, block storage, object storage, network)\n- Capacity guarantees (can they reserve resources for you?)\n\n### 3) Reliability & operations\n- Backup options (managed? policy-based?)\n- Disaster recovery patterns (cross-zone/cross-region)\n- Incident response commitments (response times by support plan)\n- Maintenance windows + impact on workloads\n\n### 4) Security & compliance\n- Certifications (ISO, SOC2, etc.)\n- IAM model (RBAC granularity, SSO/SAML/OIDC)\n- Encryption at rest/in transit (default? customer-managed keys?)\n- Audit logs + retention + exportability\n\n### 5) Networking\n- Private networking, peering, VPN options\n- Public IP management, firewall model\n- DDoS protection baseline\n- Latency expectations from your users/geos\n\n### 6) DevEx / migration\n- Terraform provider maturity\n- API quality + rate limits\n- Kubernetes offering details (if needed): upgrades, autoscaling, node pools\n- Migration help: tooling, partner support, onboarding engineer?\n\n### 7) Support quality\n- Support channels (Slack/shared channel? ticket only?)\n- Real response times in practice\n- Technical account manager availability\n- Escalation path when prod down\n\n---\n\n## Questions to ask verbatim\n- “What are the top 3 cost surprises customers face, and how avoid them?”\n- “What SLA credits exist and how often are they actually claimed?”\n- “If we onboard next month, what can break in first 90 days?”\n- “Which features are mature today vs still evolving?”\n- “Can you share a reference architecture close to our use case?”\n- “Can we run a time-boxed pilot with clear success criteria?”\n\n---\n\n## Red flags\n- Vague answers on SLA / incident process\n- “Trust us” without docs\n- No clear egress cost visibility\n- Weak IAM / audit capabilities\n- No concrete migration path\n\n---\n\n## Close the call like this\n“Great, next step: send written answers + pricing scenario + pilot proposal.  \nWe review internally, then decide go/no-go quickly.”\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also draft a **1-page call script** (opening, question flow, closing) you can read live.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01f2ca87602628a00169f1c246a124819197cbd00928500363\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":1035,"output":743,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13042,"cost":{"input":0.00181125,"output":0.010402,"cacheRead":0.0019711999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01418445}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777451585817,"responseId":"resp_01f2ca87602628a00169f1c2421dc881919362bc2ded71bcdf"}}
