rk9xrdX6-TAaDhEJUel5jIINDsF4R6hAi20VZDpRTpmtJiBKAtVY_h_2LJll1gJivBEKsctOSmpvdBaTjF691_0NIeStAdzqHrlPcDKRwmdi8qP0-c38JsQSiUHMi1eqA0GC2vb785JSPIGu6eeThoAYeLcOX-P_p-RFRZiHonRTEOzDMWuULiAPmfa611A7cJ8AaHpYHK3H-ZVffT2jeJVOlbHIr4xPgyE1y7CzRBX3DyAiJKPvvzVis7R13S_GvenTCXbCaXrUEAaDSUR\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Crafting a basic model summary**\\n\\nI see that the request is likely straightforward and might not need any tools. It feels like I need to keep things simple, almost like a “caveman mode” for communication. There seems to be a user typo, so I should check if they meant a specific model while providing baseline options. I plan to create concise bullet points covering infrastructure and hardware for serving frontier open-source models, including aspects like single and multi-node setups, networking, storage, software stack, operations, and costs.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Good q. For serve frontier open-source model, need 3 things:\n\n## 1) Hardware (GPU + RAM + network)\n\n### Small prod (7B–14B, good latency)\n- 1x–2x GPU: L40S 48GB / A100 40-80GB / H100 80GB\n- CPU: 16–32 vCPU\n- RAM: 128–256GB\n- NVMe: 1–2TB\n- Net: 10–25 Gbps\n\n### Mid prod (32B–70B, serious traffic)\n- 4x–8x GPU (80GB class best)\n- CPU: 32–64 vCPU\n- RAM: 256–512GB\n- NVMe: 4TB+\n- Net: 50–100 Gbps (important for tensor parallel)\n\n### Frontier open model (70B+ high QPS, or MoE)\n- 8x–32x H100/B200 class (cluster)\n- Multi-node with high-speed interconnect (InfiniBand/RDMA ideal)\n- RAM: 512GB–2TB per node\n- Fast shared/object storage for weights + cache\n\n---\n\n## 2) Infra blocks (must-have)\n\n- **Inference runtime**: vLLM or TGI (vLLM usually best start)\n- **Router/gateway**: OpenAI-compatible API layer, auth, rate limits\n- **Model store**: object storage (S3-like) for weights/artifacts\n- **KV/cache**: Redis for session/cache/rate-limit state\n- **Queue**: optional (Kafka/SQS/NATS) for async/batch\n- **Observability**: Prometheus + Grafana + logs + tracing\n- **Autoscaling**: K8s + HPA/KEDA (or simple VM autoscaling first)\n- **TLS + WAF**: Cloudflare/ALB/Nginx\n- **Secrets**: Vault or cloud secret manager\n- **Backup/DR**: config, prompts, finetunes, user metadata\n\n---\n\n## 3) Model memory math (quick rule)\n\n- FP16/BF16 memory ≈ **2 bytes/param**  \n  - 70B ≈ 140GB just weights (no KV, no overhead)\n- INT8 ≈ half, INT4 ≈ quarter\n- Real serving needs extra for:\n  - KV cache (big for long context)\n  - runtime overhead\n  - batching headroom\n\nSo 70B “works” on 2x80GB only in tight setup; prod comfy usually 4x+.\n\n---\n\n## 4) Performance knobs (big impact)\n\n- Quantization (AWQ/GPTQ/FP8)\n- Max context cap per tier (don’t give everyone 128k)\n- Continuous batching\n- Prefix caching\n- Speculative decoding (if supported)\n- Separate pools: cheap model vs premium model\n\n---\n\n## 5) Reliability/SRE checklist\n\n- Health checks: model loaded, tokenizer ok, warmup done\n- Graceful rolling deploy (no drop inflight req)\n- Circuit breakers + timeout budgets\n- Per-tenant quotas\n- Canary before full rollout\n- Token-level metrics: TTFT, tok/s, p95 latency, GPU util, OOM rate\n\n---\n\n## 6) Security/compliance basics\n\n- Private networking between API and GPU nodes\n- Encrypt in transit + at rest\n- Audit logs for prompts/responses access\n- PII scrubbing policy\n- Region pinning for data residency\n\n---\n\nIf you want, me make **exact sizing sheet** for your expected traffic:\n- req/min\n- avg input/output tokens\n- target p95 latency\n- max context\n- model(s) (ex: Llama 3.3 70B, Qwen3 32B)\n\nThen me give concrete node count + monthly cost range.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01f2ca87602628a00169f1e09c4ccc819183c915b43ca7eb8c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":1656,"output":890,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13810,"cost":{"input":0.002898,"output":0.01246,"cacheRead":0.00197119999999